##  About Our Lab
{{< split image="images/joinus/j2.webp" alt="" reverse="false" >}}


The research group led by **Dr. Jiangbo Wei**, Presidential Young Professor at the National University of Singapore (NUS), is affiliated with the Department of Chemistry and Department of Biological Sciences under the Faculty of Science, NUS. Dr. Wei also serves as a Research Fellow at the Cancer Science Institute of Singapore (CSI).

Our lab features a highly interdisciplinary research focus and maintains in-depth collaborations with internationally renowned research groups such as the University of Chicago and Hong Kong University of Science and Technology. We focus on **chemical biology, nucleic acid chemistry and biology, epigenetics, biochemistry and molecular biology, and bioinformatics**, dedicated to investigating the regulatory mechanisms of RNA modifications on gene expression and chromatin structure, as well as their functions in human diseases (especially cancer) and animal/plant development processes.

The lab is supported by multiple funding sources including **NUS**, the **Ministry of Education of Singapore**, and the **National Research Foundation of Singapore**, with sufficient research funding and well-equipped research facilities. Due to the recent expansion of research directions and project advancement, we are now recruiting 2-3 postdoctoral researchers globally.
{{< /split >}}


##  Principal Investigator
{{< split image="images/joinus/pi.png" alt="" reverse="true" img_style="height:32rem;" >}}

**Dr. Jiangbo Wei** joined NUS in January 2024 to establish his independent research group as a Presidential Young Professor, jointly appointed to the Department of Chemistry and Department of Biological Sciences. Since March 2025, he has served as a Research Fellow at the **Cancer Science Institute of Singapore (CSI)** and is also a core member of the National Initiative for RNA Biology & its Applications (NIRBA).

Dr. Wei received his Bachelor's degree from the College of Chemistry and Molecular Engineering, **Peking University in 2015**, and his Ph.D. from the Department of Chemistry, **University of Chicago in 2021**. During his Ph.D., he studied under the supervision of Prof. Chuan He, a renowned chemical biologist, founder of the RNA epigenetics field, and recipient of **the 2023 Wolf Prize** in Chemistry. His research focused on the molecular mechanisms of RNA modifications and functional RNAs, as well as their biological functions in various human diseases.

Dr. Wei's research achievements have been published as corresponding author or first author (including co-first author) in internationally renowned journals such as **Cell (2026), Cancer Discovery (2026), Science (2022, 2023), Molecular Cell (2018, 2019, 2023), and Nature Communications (2019, 2021, 2025)**. His research work has been cited more than 9400 times with an h-index of 36. 

[More detail About PI](../author/Jiangbo-Wei)
{{< /split >}}
 
 